  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「コバナヒメハギ」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%82%B3%E3%83%90%E3%83%8A%E3%83%92%E3%83%A1%E3%83%8F%E3%82%AE",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 106361612,
      "text": "コバナヒメハギ Polygala paniculata L. は、ヒメハギ科に属する植物。白くて小さな花を多数付ける。カスミヒメハギとも言う。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Senega paniculata」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Senega_paniculata",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1369183449,
      "text": "Senega paniculata is a species of flowering plant in the milkwort family (Polygalaceae). It is native to grasslands with altitudes between 350 and 1,700 metres. It is native to Central and South America and has been introduced to East Africa, South Asia, and Southeast Asia. It is an annual herb which has a height between 15 and 50 centimetres It is used as a medicine against snake bites and blenorrhagias. The flowers of the plant have been described as pink or white."
    }
